cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use flooded, please cite it by its DOI, 10.5281/zenodo.23302790.
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'flooded: Map Floodplains from an Elevation Model and a Stream Network'
version: 0.8.4
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23302790
abstract: Maps floodplains and unconfined valley bottoms from a digital elevation
  model and a stream network with the Valley Confinement Algorithm (VCA), keeping
  ground that is gentle, near a stream in both straight-line and slope-weighted distance,
  and low relative to it. It reads terrain rather than modelling flood flows, so it
  runs over whole watersheds for screening and planning. Fetches an elevation model
  for an area, maps preset flood levels, and attributes one floodplain to each watercourse
  that shares it, carrying per-reach flags onto the ground beside each reach. Ported
  from the bcfishpass lateral habitat pipeline (Python) with origins in the USDA VCA
  Toolbox and BlueGeo. Under active development.
